cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Autoseq-snakemake: a Snakemake pipeline suite for deep targeted sequencing of liquid biopsies"
abstract: >-
  Autoseq-snakemake is a suite of Snakemake workflows for NGS data
  analysis, aimed primarily at very deep targeted resequencing of liquid
  biopsies (cfDNA) and also supporting tumor tissue, targeted-panel,
  whole-exome and whole-genome data. The suite includes workflows for
  tumor/normal analysis, tumor-only analysis against an external normal,
  strand-duplex sequencing, whole-genome sequencing and re-analysis from
  existing alignments. The workflows share a common rule library covering
  QC, trimming, UMI processing, alignment, realignment, somatic and germline
  variant calling, copy-number and structural-variant calling, annotation
  with VEP and reporting. Each tool runs in its own Singularity container,
  and the suite is launched through a single command-line interface with
  SLURM cluster support.
